WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.781
Week 2: Greetings and First Contact. greet and take leave introduce yourself and another person choose tú or usted

2
00:00:07.781 --> 00:00:30.977
Read for the situation. Lucía llega temprano. Saluda al recepcionista con buenos días y usa usted. Después conoce a Mateo, otro estudiante, y los dos usan tú. Lucía arrives early. She greets the receptionist with good morning and uses the formal usted. Later she meets Mateo, another student, and they both use the familiar tú.

3
00:00:30.977 --> 00:00:39.718
Read again for evidence. Identify who acts, what changes, when it happens, and which words establish the relationship between events.

4
00:00:39.718 --> 00:00:44.725
Reading activities. Reading activity 3; Reading activity 4

5
00:00:44.725 --> 00:00:52.634
Retell. Without looking back, give the main idea, three supporting details, and one reasonable inference in Spanish.

6
00:00:52.634 --> 00:01:16.484
Model language. Hola, me llamo Alex. — Hello, my name is Alex. Mucho gusto, señora Rivera. — Nice to meet you, Mrs. Rivera. ¿Cómo te llamas? — What is your name? Le presento a mi compañera. — Let me introduce you to my classmate. Nos vemos mañana; que tenga buen día. — See you tomorrow; have a good day.

7
00:01:16.484 --> 00:01:26.403
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
